WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:07.020
I'm Jennifer Michele De Winter, I'm the director and co-writer of Consumers, and I also acted

2
00:00:07.020 --> 00:00:08.520
in Consumers.

3
00:00:08.520 --> 00:00:15.240
We wanted to tell a timely story about a real-world problem, but crafted through a psychological

4
00:00:15.240 --> 00:00:19.240
horror lens, something that would really grab people's attention.

5
00:00:19.240 --> 00:00:25.760
Thankfully, some amazing artists loved the concept and came on board the project.

6
00:00:25.760 --> 00:00:32.880
I was very excited to work with Mario Torres, who has worked with Chris Nolan, Guillermo del

7
00:00:32.880 --> 00:00:39.800
Toro, and David Sandberg, sound supervisor Karen Landers of Formosa Group.

8
00:00:39.800 --> 00:00:45.960
She also worked on some of the biggest horror films for Eli Roth and many others.

9
00:00:45.960 --> 00:00:49.280
And it was just an honor to have her expertise.

10
00:00:49.280 --> 00:00:54.560
I'd say David and Lotta Sandberg were some of our inspirations.

11
00:00:54.560 --> 00:01:01.280
We loved watching their films and their creative process, and it just looked like a ton of fun

12
00:01:01.280 --> 00:01:03.400
to create freely like they did.

13
00:01:03.400 --> 00:01:08.360
We also had appreciation for the greats, like Hitchcock, which you can hear in Jason

14
00:01:08.360 --> 00:01:14.120
Pelsey's music, and Kiyoshi Kurosawa and Bong Joon-ho.

15
00:01:14.120 --> 00:01:18.240
For me, directing was an honor.

16
00:01:18.240 --> 00:01:28.040
I really felt privileged that I could be in a position where I can create so closely with

17
00:01:28.040 --> 00:01:34.840
everyone and connect so closely with every part of the crew and the actors as well.

18
00:01:34.840 --> 00:01:39.840
And it was just really giving, and I really enjoyed it.

19
00:01:39.920 --> 00:01:46.360
Getting to work with Formosa Group was unreal.

20
00:01:46.360 --> 00:01:52.840
It's like I stepped into another world, and I forgot all about reality.

21
00:01:52.840 --> 00:01:54.680
It was beautiful.

22
00:01:54.680 --> 00:02:01.320
Their talents and the way they create is truly inspiring, and I just had the best time

23
00:02:01.320 --> 00:02:05.560
working with them, and I'm so honored to have them on this project.

24
00:02:05.600 --> 00:02:10.160
I'm looking forward to having audiences watch our film on the big screen.

25
00:02:10.160 --> 00:02:13.840
It'd be a great way to introduce them to the world of Consumers.

26
00:02:13.840 --> 00:02:16.000
Thank you so much.
